      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The current streetscape is hampered by inconsistent maintenance and visible infrastructure decay, creating a perception of neglect that deters large-scale private investment. The existing residential fabric, while diverse, exhibits housing stock deficiencies that reduce overall neighborhood quality and appeal to higher-income demographic targets. Furthermore, the spontaneous nature of the small shops, while charming, lacks the cohesive, professional programming often sought by major developers for long-term commercial viability. To attract the next tier of investment, the area requires immediate stabilization to align with the city's desired image of polished, high-growth urban corridors.",
      "source": "target",
